{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MfoQswAnChYpzHBMsbWVTZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture. Let me analyze the key data:\n\n**APC 0 → APC 300 scaling:**\n- Cells: 1.90B → 811M (2.35x reduction)\n- Constraint Instances: 1.13B → 505M (2.23x reduction)  \n- Bus Interaction Messages: 965M → 448M (2.15x reduction)\n\nBut **STARK (excl. trace)**: 2.17s → 2.46s (actually INCREASED by ~13%!)\n\nThis is the core problem. The GPU prover is not scaling with the workload reduction.\n \nDigging into the constraint phase breakdown, I see the real culprit: Round 0 is exploding from 0.18s to 0.66s—a 267% jump that completely dominates the slowdown. Meanwhile, LogUp GKR actually scales well with the reduced workload, dropping 22%, but it's being overwhelmed by Round 0's catastrophic performance. The openings phase also degrades, though WHIR shows some improvement.\n\nThe pattern is clear: Round 0, Stacked Reduction, and MLE Rounds all get worse as APC count increases, which points to the AIR instance explosion (99 to 623) as the real bottleneck. More APCs means more instances to process, and these components aren't handling that scaling well.\n\nLet me save these metrics as my baseline and then dig into profiling to understand where the per-instance overhead is coming from.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3037,"cache_read_input_tokens":30246,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3037},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f2238e8-ef27-4ab7-979f-317ec3807970","uuid":"82287a0a-7446-4a8c-bea9-8543217b240b"}
