{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017aeXQZJ27XcJ44K2pwUw8V","type":"tool_result","content":"5://! new allocations happen before the current stream is synchronized, physical peak memory can\n58:        gkr_input::TraceInteractionMeta, round0::evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu,\n72:/// Logup interaction evaluations for GKR input\n87:use round0::evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu;\n90:/// instead of the monomial kernel for high num_y traces.\n91:/// This ratio can be tuned. Currently it is set to prefer the monomial kernel except for the\n96:pub(crate) fn air_width_for_mat(need_rot: bool, mat_width: usize) -> u32 {\n145:    // There's no stride threshold for `interactions_layout` because there's no univariate skip for\n149:    // Grind to increase soundness of random sampling for LogUp\n174:        .emit_metrics_with_label(\"prover.before_gkr_input_evals\");\n189:    // Set memory limit for batch MLE based on inputs buffer size\n206:    while xi.len() != l_skip + n_global {\n215:    // not include the kernel times for the actual folding\n239:        for (i, coeffs) in sp_0_polys[..2 * num_traces].iter().enumerate() {\n240:            for (j, &c_j) in coeffs.coeffs().iter().enumerate().take(sp_0_deg + 1) {\n243:                // - sp_coeffs_mat allocated for width\n250:        for (eq, row) in zip(eq_evals, s_evals.values.chunks_mut(width)) {\n251:            for x in row {\n296:        for (j, batch_coeff) in sp_coeffs.iter_mut().enumerate().take(sp_0_deg + 1) {\n297:            for (&mu, poly) in zip(mus, polys) {\n302:        for (eq, x) in zip(eq_evals, &mut s_evals) {\n347:    for round in 1..=n_max {\n353:        for &eval in &batch_s_evals {\n375:    for (need_rot, openings) in need_rot_per_trace.iter().zip(column_openings.iter()) {\n376:        for (claim, claim_rot) in column_openings_by_rot(&openings[0], *need_rot) {\n381:    for (need_rot, openings) in need_rot_per_trace.iter().zip(column_openings.iter()) {\n382:        for part in openings.iter().skip(1) {\n383:            for (claim, claim_rot) in column_openings_by_rot(part, *need_rot) {\n432:    /// Beta powers on device for logup MLE rounds.\n437:    // n_T => segment tree of eq(xi[j..1+n_T]) for j=1..={n_T-round+1} in _reverse_ layout\n441:    // Evaluations on hypercube only, for round 0\n466:    /// Memory limit for batch MLE intermediate buffers (set after GKR input eval)\n528:        // Collect interaction metadata for GPU execution (evaluations still run on CPU for now).\n595:    // PERF[jpw]: we could return evals and batch zerocheck poly by degree before interpolating.\n596:    // Cannot do it for logup because we need to calculate the sum claims.\n604:            .emit_metrics_with_label(\"prover.batch_constraints.before_round0\");\n615:        // Precompute lambda combinations for all AIRs with monomials\n617:        for (air_idx, air_pk) in self.pk.per_air.iter().enumerate() {\n640:                    for interaction_idx in 0..num_interactions {\n647:                        for bit in &mut b_vec {\n673:        // Precompute logup combinations for all traces with interaction monomials\n674:        for (trace_idx, (air_idx, _)) in ctx.per_trace.iter().enumerate() {\n693:        // PERF[jpw]: we could also build the layers for different n in a transposed way using\n695:        for &n in &self.n_per_trace {\n722:        // All (numer, denom) pairs per present AIR for logup, followed by 1 zerocheck poly per\n728:            .expect(\"lambda powers must be set before round-0 evaluation\");\n730:        // Loop through one AIR at a time; it is more efficient to do everything for one AIR\n732:        for (trace_idx, ((air_idx, air_ctx), &n, selectors_cube, public_values, eq_3bs)) in izip!(\n741:            debug!(\"starting batch constraints for air_idx={air_idx} (trace_idx={trace_idx})\");\n764:            for committed in &air_ctx.cached_mains {","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MQvLWwmfYrQkKhNwfzkjse","sess