in ctx.per_trace:\n    evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu(this_air)  // GPU kernel\n    evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu(this_air)  // GPU kernel\n    CPU: polynomial conversion and storage\n```\n\n**Opportunities for parallelization:**\n\n1. **Kernel Batching Across AIRs (Multi-Stream):**\n   - Launch constraint evaluation kernels for multiple AIRs concurrently on separate streams\n   - Constraint evaluation kernels have independent GPU memory (selectors, matrices differ)\n   - **Note:** No data dependencies between AIRs until polynomial batching\n\n2. **Early Stage (Pre-Round-0):**\n   - Lambda combinations (lines 617-624) could be computed in parallel for different AIRs\n   - Logup combinations (lines 674-691) could be parallelized similarly\n   - Selector cube preparation (line 729) per-AIR\n\n3. **Interaction Evaluation Batching:**\n   - Multiple `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` calls could overlap\n   - Each AIR's interaction evaluation is independent until stacking\n\n4. **Round K Evaluation:**\n   - Lines 1031-1038: Per-trace/AIR evaluations in round K could use separate streams\n   - \"Late eval\" and \"early eval\" batches could run concurrently on different streams\n   - Synchronization point: before polynomial batching in `compute_batch_s`\n\n**Constraints on Parallelism:**\n- **Synchronization bottleneck:** CPU must convert GPU results to host for polynomial operations (lines 792-827, 848-879)\n- **Data dependency:** All AIR constraint results must be collected before batch polynomial (line 309-324)\n- **Transcript ordering:** Observations must stay sequential for Fiat-Shamir consistency (lines 275-276, 320, 354)\n- **Memory:** Parallel kernels could increase peak GPU memory due to buffering\n\n### 9. **CPU Backend Reference (for comparison)**\n\n`/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/stark-backend/src/prover/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (lines 40-200):\n- Uses `par_iter()` for interaction evaluation across AIRs (lines 107-137)\n- Rayon parallelism for per-heigh